  "result": "Perfect! All **403 tests pass** (373 existing + 30 new bulk discount tests).\n\n## Bulk Discount Implementation Summary\n\n**Modified: `src/totals.js`**\n- Updated `lineDiscount()` function to apply an extra 2.5% discount on lines with qty \u2265 10\n- Bulk discount is applied after the primary discount (line's own or tier discount)\n- VAT is calculated on the amount after both discounts combined\n- Discount calculation order:\n  1. Primary discount: `qty * unitPrice * (discountPercent / 100)`\n  2. After primary: remaining amount\n  3. Bulk discount: `remainingAmount * 0.025` (only if qty \u2265 10)\n  4. Total discount returned: primary + bulk\n\n**New Tests: `test/totals.test.js`** (30 test cases)\n- Bulk discount boundary conditions (qty < 10 vs qty \u2265 10)\n- Bulk discount with primary discounts and VAT\n- Bulk discount with multiple lines\n- Interaction with tier discounts\n- Rounding behavior\n- Edge cases: zero amounts, 100% primary discount\n\n**Updated Tests**\n- `test/invoices.test.js`: Fixed 6 tests to account for bulk discount\n- `test/render.test.js`: Fixed 2 render tests to show correct totals with bulk discount\n\n**Behavior**\n- Lines with 10+ units automatically receive an additional 2.5% discount\n- Discount is included in the invoice's total discount amount\n- VAT calculation respects bulk discount (tax applies only after both discounts)\n- Works seamlessly with tier discounts and explicit line discounts",
